atlas execution

architecture work-graph
  canonical_name WorkGraph
  family execution
  domain Execution
  layer execution
  semantic_question What durable work exists, with what dependencies and lifecycle?
  purpose WorkGraph-backed durable missions with causal dependency semantics; distinct from queue scheduling.
  maturity implemented
  node_types WorkItem
  node_types Mission
  edge_types depends_on
  state_types queued
  state_types running
  state_types done
  state_types failed
  invariant dependency carries causal execution semantics, not mere ordering
  invariant a node's family must be registered as routable, or it is rejected (native + python parity)
  forbidden_inference queue priority -> durability guarantee
  command BonfyreQueue
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/work_graph.py
  source_path engine/core/src/workgraph.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_workgraph.h
  witness engine/core/tests/routable_family_test.c
  known_gap native WorkGraph is mature and now family-routing-checked; native Occurrence and Resource/Actor persistence, plane replay, and supervisor call-site replacement are the open native-absorption items (Python authority not yet retired)
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_work_graph.py
  source_lineage run6 control-plane retrospective

architecture occurrence-spine
  canonical_name OccurrenceSpine
  family execution
  domain Execution / Causal Time
  layer execution
  semantic_question What actually happened, when, as an ordered causal spine?
  purpose External events and occurrences folded into an ordered spine; the backbone the control plane reasons over.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Occurrence
  node_types ExternalEvent
  edge_types precedes
  forbidden_inference retrieval time -> event time (timestamps must not collapse)
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/external_events.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/ingest_github_notifications.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/migrate_run6.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_external_events.py
  source_lineage run6 control-plane retrospective

architecture transport-phenotype
  canonical_name TransportPhenotypeGraph
  family execution
  domain Execution / Transport
  layer execution/transport
  semantic_question By which carrier does a hop run, and what does each carrier add?
  purpose Direct subprocess, MCP (adds a signed receipt), external HTTP (ForeignTwin, rights-gated). Transport is orthogonal to computational form.
  maturity measured
  node_types Transport
  node_types Hop
  edge_types carries
  internal_calculus direct|mcp|external carrier selection
  invariant the same hop yields a byte-identical digest across direct and MCP; MCP adds a receipt
  forbidden_inference MCP receipt present -> different computation occurred
  computational_form durable
  command BonfyreProject
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/transport.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_transport.py
  source_lineage MCP native_tool_invoke work
